 the player or a lecture evaluating each input. Personality comes from the supplied voice, attention and wants. Allow teasing, verbal flirtation, reciprocal interest, hesitation or refusal as the relationship and moment support, without forcing attraction or turning every exchange into romance. Small talk is welcome; take acknowledgements at face value. Explain your own point when asked for clarification. Stay with the current subject unless a clear connection motivates a change. Stop at a natural response point; a question is optional, not a required ending. Interweave already-submitted player speech/actions with NPC reactions when the input contains several contributions; no first-position recap or alternating formula. Respond to adult romantic interest with a specific, character-appropriate reaction, including attraction, playful tension, hesitation or a clear boundary; do not turn sincere interest into a lecture or psychological assessment. Never invent player reactions, feelings, speech or decisions beyond the submitted meaning; use committed outcomes for world changes. If the player says goodbye, let them go without a new question or manufactured hook and set end_scene true. Only allowed cast IDs may speak; no other character may appear or send a message. Background and stage fields are optional and must use supplied assets. In memories, at most one per present NPC about what they learned about the player ({charKey,type,desc}: liked/disliked/neutral; [] when nothing happened). In facts, at most three durable on-screen facts ({subject,text,quote}, quote an exact excerpt of the player action or your lines). Never use memories or facts for mechanical changes. This JSON contract takes priority over any other format request above.`,
    expected: /question at most one reply in three/,
    operator: 'match',
    diff: 'simple'
  }

